1
00:00:00,333 --> 00:00:05,133
Whenever your phone rings, do you worry that it is another recovery call?

2
00:00:05,613 --> 00:00:08,253
Forty calls, fifty calls a day.

3
00:00:08,453 --> 00:00:10,133
And WhatsApp messages in between.

4
00:00:10,413 --> 00:00:13,333
“Make the payment today.” “Our team is coming to your house.”

5
00:00:13,533 --> 00:00:14,613
“There will be a police case.”

6
00:00:15,133 --> 00:00:18,333
You reach a point where even the phone ringing frightens you, right?

7
00:00:18,693 --> 00:00:21,453
An unknown number appears and your heart starts racing.

8
00:00:21,813 --> 00:00:23,173
What if your family finds out?

9
00:00:23,373 --> 00:00:24,893
What if they call your office?

10
00:00:25,253 --> 00:00:27,373
Even when you go to bed, these thoughts keep running through your mind.

11
00:00:27,853 --> 00:00:30,493
Okay. First, take a deep breath.

12
00:00:30,933 --> 00:00:33,533
Let us calmly understand your situation.

13
00:00:34,053 --> 00:00:37,293
What actually happens when you cannot pay your credit card bill?

14
00:00:37,693 --> 00:00:39,213
What rights does the bank have?

15
00:00:39,613 --> 00:00:41,133
What protections do you have?

16
00:00:41,613 --> 00:00:43,613
How should you handle recovery calls?

17
00:00:44,013 --> 00:00:48,573
What does settlement mean? And how can you rebuild your credit score afterwards?

18
00:00:49,053 --> 00:00:50,333
Let us talk through everything, one step at a time.

19
00:00:50,653 --> 00:00:53,933
Simply, as if we were sitting across from each other and having a conversation.

20
00:00:58,527 --> 00:01:00,207
First, let us be clear about one thing.

21
00:01:00,687 --> 00:01:05,247
If you are in a position to make the payment, paying on time is better for you.

22
00:01:05,647 --> 00:01:08,531
This video is for people whose income has genuinely fallen,

23
00:01:08,531 --> 00:01:12,393
whose medical expenses have increased, who are trapped in credit card rotation,

24
00:01:12,393 --> 00:01:15,327
and who cannot manage their bills despite trying everything.

25
00:01:15,807 --> 00:01:18,767
Because saying, “I will not pay,” is one thing.

26
00:01:19,047 --> 00:01:21,847
Saying, “I cannot pay right now,” is another.

27
00:01:22,287 --> 00:01:26,127
First, be honest with yourself about your actual situation.

28
00:01:26,767 --> 00:01:29,407
Usually, this problem does not become serious all at once.

29
00:01:29,807 --> 00:01:31,207
First, there is an emergency.

30
00:01:31,607 --> 00:01:34,087
It could be a hospital bill or a job loss.

31
00:01:34,367 --> 00:01:36,287
Or payments may have stopped coming into your business.

32
00:01:36,727 --> 00:01:40,127
“Let us use the card this month, and clear it next month,” we think.

33
00:01:40,607 --> 00:01:42,247
Then another expense arrives next month.

34
00:01:42,607 --> 00:01:46,607
We arrange money from another card to pay the first card's bill.

35
00:01:47,007 --> 00:01:48,327
Then we pay the minimum due.

36
00:01:48,607 --> 00:01:49,927
Then we take a small loan.

37
00:01:50,207 --> 00:01:51,647
Then we turn to another loan app.

38
00:01:52,167 --> 00:01:56,847
Before we know it, the salary is coming in, but there is no money left in our hands.

39
00:01:57,327 --> 00:02:00,287
“I earn this much, so where is all my money going?”

40
00:02:00,527 --> 00:02:03,287
You wonder that, do you not? This is where we need to pause.

41
00:02:03,767 --> 00:02:08,887
When we cover old borrowing with new borrowing, are we actually solving the problem?

42
00:02:09,167 --> 00:02:11,327
Or are we simply pushing it into next month?

43
00:02:11,807 --> 00:02:13,847
That question may feel uncomfortable.

44
00:02:14,167 --> 00:02:16,487
But that is where clarity begins.

45
00:02:17,127 --> 00:02:21,887
One more thing. Being in financial difficulty does not reduce your worth.

46
00:02:22,327 --> 00:02:25,327
An overdue bill does not make you a bad person.

47
00:02:25,807 --> 00:02:28,767
You are facing a serious financial problem.

48
00:02:29,127 --> 00:02:31,287
To handle it, you need a plan.

49
00:02:31,487 --> 00:02:34,087
You need support. And you need correct information.

50
00:02:34,527 --> 00:02:37,007
You do not have to make decisions out of shame.

51
00:02:37,567 --> 00:02:40,367
So, what is your first priority in this situation?

52
00:02:40,807 --> 00:02:46,087
Food, medicines, rent, your children's school expenses, and basic needs at home.

53
00:02:46,607 --> 00:02:47,807
Think about this for a moment.

54
00:02:48,247 --> 00:02:53,890
If you pay to reduce a recovery caller's pressure and have no money left for medicines,

55
00:02:53,890 --> 00:02:55,447
is that a workable plan?

56
00:02:55,598 --> 00:03:00,182
First, write down your monthly income, essential expenses,

57
00:03:00,182 --> 00:03:03,898
and what you can realistically afford to repay.

58
00:03:04,258 --> 00:03:05,678
Do not just calculate it in your head.

59
00:03:06,058 --> 00:03:08,458
Write it on paper or in your phone notes.

60
00:03:08,818 --> 00:03:11,178
Once you see the numbers, your situation becomes clearer.

61
00:03:11,598 --> 00:03:16,898
Rather than hoping, “I will somehow manage,” a realistic budget will help you more.

62
00:03:19,611 --> 00:03:23,031
Okay. Now, the question that frightens many people the most.

63
00:03:23,451 --> 00:03:26,371
“Will the police arrest me if I cannot pay my credit card bill?”

64
00:03:27,031 --> 00:03:30,213
When genuine financial difficulty prevents you from paying,

65
00:03:30,213 --> 00:03:32,371
it is generally a civil recovery matter.

66
00:03:32,871 --> 00:03:36,871
Missing a payment alone does not automatically prove cheating.

67
00:03:37,371 --> 00:03:39,352
A cheating allegation requires looking at

68
00:03:39,352 --> 00:03:41,671
facts such as dishonest intention and deception.

69
00:03:42,171 --> 00:03:43,571
Was there fraud from the beginning?

70
00:03:43,871 --> 00:03:46,971
Did you submit false documents? Did you deliberately mislead anyone?

71
00:03:47,371 --> 00:03:48,871
These are separate questions.

72
00:03:49,271 --> 00:03:51,821
The Supreme Court has also explained the difference

73
00:03:51,821 --> 00:03:54,171
between a mere breach of contract and cheating.

74
00:03:54,671 --> 00:03:55,893
So, a caller saying,

75
00:03:55,893 --> 00:04:00,171
“We will file a criminal case,” does not establish the legal position.

76
00:04:00,671 --> 00:04:05,671
At the same time, do not say, “It is a civil matter, so nothing can happen.”

77
00:04:06,171 --> 00:04:08,171
The bank can start a legal recovery process.

78
00:04:08,671 --> 00:04:12,171
It can send a notice. It can approach a court through the applicable procedure.

79
00:04:12,671 --> 00:04:14,671
A court order can have consequences.

80
00:04:15,171 --> 00:04:19,453
So, do not ignore a genuine legal notice, court summons,

81
00:04:19,453 --> 00:04:21,671
or arbitration communication.

82
00:04:22,171 --> 00:04:26,671
Verify it. If necessary, get help from a lawyer or legal aid.

83
00:04:27,171 --> 00:04:28,671
Remember one thing here.

84
00:04:29,171 --> 00:04:32,671
How loudly a caller speaks is not legal proof.

85
00:04:33,171 --> 00:04:36,671
Actual documents, actual facts, and the actual procedure matter.

86
00:04:37,171 --> 00:04:38,671
What about a bounced cheque?

87
00:04:39,171 --> 00:04:42,171
Or a failed auto-debit? Those are separate legal issues too.

88
00:04:42,671 --> 00:04:47,904
Whether a particular law applies depends on the transaction, mandate, notice,

89
00:04:47,904 --> 00:04:49,671
and the facts of the case.

90
00:04:49,671 --> 00:04:55,171
Do not assume that no law can apply simply because it involves a credit card.

91
00:04:55,671 --> 00:04:59,671
Read the notice you receive and respond appropriately.

92
00:05:00,171 --> 00:05:03,641
Now, another common fear.

93
00:05:04,141 --> 00:05:05,641
“I do not have just one card.

94
00:05:06,141 --> 00:05:07,641
I owe four or five banks.

95
00:05:08,141 --> 00:05:09,641
What if they all put pressure on me?”

96
00:05:10,141 --> 00:05:13,641
Yes, multiple accounts can feel mentally overwhelming.

97
00:05:14,141 --> 00:05:16,141
One bank's call ends and another bank calls.

98
00:05:16,641 --> 00:05:19,641
You may even lose track of how much you owe on each account.

99
00:05:19,641 --> 00:05:22,141
First, make a simple list.

100
00:05:22,641 --> 00:05:27,141
The card issuer's name, outstanding amount, due date, last payment date,

101
00:05:27,141 --> 00:05:28,641
and complaint reference.

102
00:05:29,141 --> 00:05:33,141
Record any legal communication too, and keep everything in one place.

103
00:05:33,641 --> 00:05:35,641
Track every account separately.

104
00:05:36,141 --> 00:05:40,141
Settling with one bank does not settle your other accounts.

105
00:05:40,282 --> 00:05:45,002
Do not assume the bank will avoid court just because the amount is small.

106
00:05:45,482 --> 00:05:49,568
Recovery decisions depend on the account's facts, the issuer's policy,

107
00:05:49,568 --> 00:05:51,202
and available legal options.

108
00:05:51,642 --> 00:05:55,282
Your plan should not depend on guessing, “They will not do anything.”

109
00:05:55,682 --> 00:05:57,689
It should be based on, “Whatever communication arrives,

110
00:05:57,689 --> 00:05:59,002
I will respond in an organised way.”

111
00:05:59,122 --> 00:06:00,642
That is the confidence you need.

112
00:06:03,262 --> 00:06:05,182
Now, let us talk about your statement.

113
00:06:05,582 --> 00:06:07,182
You have stopped using the card.

114
00:06:07,582 --> 00:06:09,062
The card has even been blocked.

115
00:06:09,382 --> 00:06:11,062
Yet the balance keeps increasing.

116
00:06:11,502 --> 00:06:14,182
“What is this? I have not spent anything new, have I?”

117
00:06:14,382 --> 00:06:18,942
That is what you wonder. Blocking the card may stop new transactions.

118
00:06:19,262 --> 00:06:21,891
But it does not automatically stop applicable

119
00:06:21,891 --> 00:06:25,222
interest and charges on the existing outstanding balance.

120
00:06:25,582 --> 00:06:27,382
That is where the confusion begins.

121
00:06:27,822 --> 00:06:29,782
How much is the purchase balance in your statement?

122
00:06:30,142 --> 00:06:33,022
How much are the finance charges? What is the late payment fee?

123
00:06:33,302 --> 00:06:36,382
What are the taxes? How have your previous payments been adjusted?

124
00:06:36,822 --> 00:06:41,702
Looking only at the total without checking the breakdown just increases your fear.

125
00:06:42,222 --> 00:06:43,622
Let us take a simple example.

126
00:06:44,102 --> 00:06:45,902
Suppose the outstanding amount is one lakh.

127
00:06:46,382 --> 00:06:50,462
At three percent monthly interest, that would be roughly three thousand in interest.

128
00:06:50,982 --> 00:06:53,542
This is only an example to explain the idea.

129
00:06:54,022 --> 00:06:57,862
Check your card's terms for your actual rate and calculation method.

130
00:06:58,342 --> 00:07:01,178
When applicable fees and taxes are added,

131
00:07:01,178 --> 00:07:04,982
a small payment may not reduce the principal very much.

132
00:07:05,422 --> 00:07:09,702
Then you wonder, “I am paying, so why is the balance not going down?”

133
00:07:10,142 --> 00:07:13,742
Paying the minimum due does not mean the full bill has been cleared.

134
00:07:14,142 --> 00:07:17,302
Finance charges may continue on the remaining balance.

135
00:07:17,702 --> 00:07:20,902
The interest-free period may also be affected according to your card's terms.

136
00:07:21,422 --> 00:07:24,702
But do not assume the minimum due is completely useless.

137
00:07:25,182 --> 00:07:29,662
Paying the required minimum on time can help keep the account from becoming overdue.

138
00:07:30,102 --> 00:07:33,296
The problem is that repeatedly paying only the minimum

139
00:07:33,296 --> 00:07:35,662
can keep the debt going for a long time.

140
00:07:36,062 --> 00:07:38,942
So, if you can afford it, paying in full is better.

141
00:07:39,342 --> 00:07:43,782
Otherwise, talk to the bank about a workable repayment option.

142
00:07:44,302 --> 00:07:45,822
There is another important protection.

143
00:07:46,222 --> 00:07:49,406
Under RBI credit card rules, unpaid taxes, levies,

144
00:07:49,406 --> 00:07:54,182
and charges must not be capitalised to charge or compound interest on them.

145
00:07:54,542 --> 00:07:55,993
Similarly, interest, taxes,

146
00:07:55,993 --> 00:08:01,582
and other charges must not be included in credit-limit usage calculations for levying an over-limit fee.

147
00:08:01,742 --> 00:08:03,142
RBI has clarified this.

148
00:08:03,662 --> 00:08:06,281
So, if you see an incorrect charge in your statement,

149
00:08:06,281 --> 00:08:09,542
do not assume it must be correct just because the bank charged it.

150
00:08:09,902 --> 00:08:12,622
Ask for a written breakdown and raise a dispute.

151
00:08:13,142 --> 00:08:17,142
Does settlement mean all interest and penalties will be removed?

152
00:08:17,622 --> 00:08:21,222
In some cases, the bank may agree to waive part of the amount.

153
00:08:21,542 --> 00:08:23,382
But that is not an automatic right.

154
00:08:23,742 --> 00:08:27,463
It depends on your hardship, the account's situation, the bank's policy,

155
00:08:27,463 --> 00:08:28,342
and the approval.

156
00:08:28,535 --> 00:08:33,035
Do not assume, “Because there is an RBI rule, they must give me a discount.”

157
00:08:33,535 --> 00:08:37,041
Understand your actual spending, payments, interest,

158
00:08:37,041 --> 00:08:39,535
and charges before making a proposal.

159
00:08:39,535 --> 00:08:42,035
Clarity helps during negotiation.

160
00:08:44,492 --> 00:08:46,992
Now, we need to talk about your salary account.

161
00:08:47,492 --> 00:08:50,992
Is your salary account with the same bank where your credit card is overdue?

162
00:08:50,992 --> 00:08:55,992
If so, check your agreement for lien or set-off clauses.

163
00:08:55,992 --> 00:08:57,492
What does set-off mean?

164
00:08:57,492 --> 00:08:59,684
Under applicable terms and law,

165
00:08:59,684 --> 00:09:04,492
the bank may adjust money in your account with it against your dues.

166
00:09:04,992 --> 00:09:09,559
Do not blindly assume, “My savings account and credit card are separate,

167
00:09:09,559 --> 00:09:11,082
so there is no problem.”

168
00:09:11,582 --> 00:09:14,582
Some card agreements explicitly include these rights.

169
00:09:15,082 --> 00:09:20,582
So, plan ahead for the money you rely on for essential expenses.

170
00:09:20,582 --> 00:09:24,582
If necessary, seek advice about changing your salary banking arrangement.

171
00:09:24,582 --> 00:09:30,582
But changing accounts does not permanently protect your money from legal recovery.

172
00:09:30,582 --> 00:09:35,582
You must comply with court orders and valid legal obligations.

173
00:09:35,582 --> 00:09:37,622
What is our purpose here?

174
00:09:37,622 --> 00:09:40,716
To understand the situation and plan ahead

175
00:09:40,716 --> 00:09:44,622
so household expenses are not unexpectedly disrupted.

176
00:09:44,622 --> 00:09:50,638
Okay. Now, how should you communicate with the bank?

177
00:09:50,638 --> 00:09:51,880
When the calls keep coming,

178
00:09:51,880 --> 00:09:54,638
you may feel like switching off your phone and disappearing.

179
00:09:54,638 --> 00:09:56,638
“I will not answer anyone for a few days.

180
00:09:56,638 --> 00:09:58,638
At least I will have some peace,” you may think.

181
00:09:58,638 --> 00:10:00,638
That feeling is understandable.

182
00:10:00,638 --> 00:10:04,638
But complete silence does not explain your situation to the bank.

183
00:10:04,638 --> 00:10:06,638
It does not resolve the problem either.

184
00:10:06,638 --> 00:10:10,638
Instead, send a clear written communication.

185
00:10:10,638 --> 00:10:13,297
Verify the grievance officer's or nodal

186
00:10:13,297 --> 00:10:16,638
officer's contact on the bank's official website.

187
00:10:16,638 --> 00:10:18,638
Send a hardship email there.

188
00:10:18,638 --> 00:10:20,638
You do not need fancy English.

189
00:10:20,638 --> 00:10:22,638
Explain your actual situation clearly.

190
00:10:22,638 --> 00:10:24,638
“My income has fallen.”

191
00:10:24,638 --> 00:10:27,638
“Medical expenses have made it difficult to manage the current payment.”

192
00:10:27,638 --> 00:10:31,638
“I am available to discuss repayment options.”

193
00:10:31,638 --> 00:10:35,638
“After essential expenses, this is the amount I can afford each month.”

194
00:10:35,638 --> 00:10:37,638
State the facts like this.

195
00:10:37,638 --> 00:10:40,638
Do not promise an amount you cannot afford.

196
00:10:40,638 --> 00:10:44,638
It is easy to say, “I will pay tomorrow,” just to end the call.

197
00:10:44,638 --> 00:10:47,638
But tomorrow, the same pressure returns, right?

198
00:10:47,638 --> 00:10:49,638
Honestly say, “I cannot commit to that amount.

199
00:10:49,638 --> 00:10:52,638
I need a workable option.”

200
00:10:52,638 --> 00:10:54,798
A reduced EMI.

201
00:10:54,798 --> 00:10:56,798
A repayment plan. Restructuring.

202
00:10:56,798 --> 00:11:00,798
Settlement. Ask in writing which options apply to your situation.

203
00:11:00,798 --> 00:11:03,798
You can also say that you prefer written communication.

204
00:11:03,798 --> 00:11:07,264
But requesting communication only by email does not

205
00:11:07,264 --> 00:11:10,798
mean the bank loses permission to make lawful calls.

206
00:11:10,798 --> 00:11:12,798
That request is a communication preference.

207
00:11:12,798 --> 00:11:15,798
The protections against harassment are a separate matter.

208
00:11:16,384 --> 00:11:20,224
Email copies, attachments, acknowledgements, and complaint IDs.

209
00:11:20,304 --> 00:11:23,504
Save them all. Create a folder and keep them together.

210
00:11:24,024 --> 00:11:26,304
The email you sent is a useful record.

211
00:11:26,584 --> 00:11:30,184
But it is not a shield that automatically stops a court case.

212
00:11:30,744 --> 00:11:34,584
It documents your communication, hardship, and cooperation.

213
00:11:37,228 --> 00:11:39,428
Now, let us talk about recovery agents.

214
00:11:39,988 --> 00:11:41,868
They may contact you about payment.

215
00:11:42,068 --> 00:11:46,616
But insulting, threatening, or publicly humiliating you during recovery,

216
00:11:46,616 --> 00:11:50,028
or intruding on your family's privacy, is not allowed.

217
00:11:50,628 --> 00:11:55,552
Under RBI instructions, threatening or anonymous calls, inappropriate messages,

218
00:11:55,552 --> 00:11:58,108
and persistent harassment are prohibited.

219
00:11:58,818 --> 00:12:01,284
Calls to recover overdue dues must not be made before

220
00:12:01,284 --> 00:12:03,658
eight in the morning or after seven in the evening.

221
00:12:04,098 --> 00:12:07,778
Does that mean anything is acceptable between eight and seven?

222
00:12:08,858 --> 00:12:12,858
No. Following the time limit does not make harassment acceptable.

223
00:12:14,418 --> 00:12:17,498
“We will tell your neighbours.” “We will speak in front of everyone at your office.”

224
00:12:17,898 --> 00:12:19,218
“We will trouble your family.”

225
00:12:19,778 --> 00:12:21,463
If you face this kind of pressure,

226
00:12:21,463 --> 00:12:24,338
you do not have to accept it as a normal recovery process.

227
00:12:24,898 --> 00:12:26,938
Calmly ask, “What is your name?

228
00:12:27,298 --> 00:12:30,138
What is the agency's name? Which bank are you representing?

229
00:12:30,498 --> 00:12:33,218
Please send your authorisation details through an official email.”

230
00:12:34,088 --> 00:12:37,688
If they speak loudly, you do not have to raise your voice too.

231
00:12:38,168 --> 00:12:40,288
Your goal is not to win an argument.

232
00:12:40,808 --> 00:12:43,848
It is to document the situation and handle it through the correct channel.

233
00:12:44,288 --> 00:12:48,128
If necessary, say, “I have explained my hardship to the bank in writing.

234
00:12:48,608 --> 00:12:51,128
I will discuss payment options through the official channel.

235
00:12:51,608 --> 00:12:53,288
Please do not use threatening language.”

236
00:12:53,728 --> 00:12:55,808
Short. Clear. That is enough.

237
00:12:56,658 --> 00:12:59,978
What if you get a WhatsApp message asking you to share your live location?

238
00:13:00,898 --> 00:13:01,898
First, pause.

239
00:13:02,538 --> 00:13:05,978
You do not have to share your location just because an unknown person asks.

240
00:13:06,418 --> 00:13:10,258
Officially verify their identity and bank authorisation.

241
00:13:10,858 --> 00:13:15,418
Never share an OTP, PIN, password, or card details.

242
00:13:15,858 --> 00:13:19,898
Asking for your location alone does not prove that someone is fake.

243
00:13:20,138 --> 00:13:23,858
But there is no need to give personal information without verification.

244
00:13:24,638 --> 00:13:27,918
What if a message says, “Our agent visited, but your door was locked”?

245
00:13:28,628 --> 00:13:30,588
Check the facts you know.

246
00:13:30,948 --> 00:13:33,268
Who actually visited? At what time?

247
00:13:33,468 --> 00:13:36,948
Which agency? Confirm through the bank's official channel.

248
00:13:37,428 --> 00:13:39,828
Do not assume every message is genuine.

249
00:13:40,228 --> 00:13:42,788
And do not dismiss every message as fake.

250
00:13:43,148 --> 00:13:44,908
That is a sensible approach.

251
00:13:45,668 --> 00:13:49,468
What if a message says, “Click this link to see your legal notice”?

252
00:13:50,108 --> 00:13:52,348
Do not immediately tap an unknown link.

253
00:13:52,748 --> 00:13:57,708
Confirm through the bank app, official website, or verified customer care.

254
00:13:58,228 --> 00:14:00,788
Legal communication can also arrive electronically.

255
00:14:01,148 --> 00:14:04,988
So, do not assume it is fake just because it came through WhatsApp or email.

256
00:14:05,124 --> 00:14:07,124
Who sent it? Are there case details?

257
00:14:07,124 --> 00:14:10,124
Can you verify the court or the lawyer's information?

258
00:14:10,124 --> 00:14:11,124
Check these things.

259
00:14:11,124 --> 00:14:15,124
Spending two minutes verifying is better than clicking out of fear.

260
00:14:15,124 --> 00:14:18,184
Now, what if someone actually comes to your house?

261
00:14:18,184 --> 00:14:20,184
First, stay calm.

262
00:14:20,184 --> 00:14:24,184
If you feel uncomfortable, you do not have to invite them inside.

263
00:14:24,184 --> 00:14:26,184
Ask for an ID card.

264
00:14:26,184 --> 00:14:28,184
Ask for the bank's authorisation letter.

265
00:14:28,184 --> 00:14:30,184
Verify which account the visit concerns.

266
00:14:30,184 --> 00:14:33,184
Speak only in a place where you feel safe.

267
00:14:33,184 --> 00:14:37,184
If needed, ask a trusted person to stay with you.

268
00:14:37,184 --> 00:14:39,184
“Sign right now.” “Give me cash.”

269
00:14:39,184 --> 00:14:43,184
“Give me your phone.” Do not immediately react to this kind of pressure.

270
00:14:43,184 --> 00:14:45,184
Read and understand any document.

271
00:14:45,184 --> 00:14:49,184
Sign only after getting advice if you need it.

272
00:14:49,184 --> 00:14:52,173
If there is force, a physical threat, or immediate danger,

273
00:14:52,173 --> 00:14:54,184
call the emergency number, one one two.

274
00:14:54,184 --> 00:14:56,184
Your safety comes first.

275
00:14:56,184 --> 00:15:01,184
But an authorised recovery visit is not automatically illegal.

276
00:15:01,184 --> 00:15:05,184
The person's conduct and whether the proper process is followed are what matter.

277
00:15:05,184 --> 00:15:08,224
Now, how do you complain about harassment?

278
00:15:08,224 --> 00:15:10,224
Note the dates.

279
00:15:10,224 --> 00:15:12,224
Save the phone numbers.

280
00:15:12,224 --> 00:15:14,224
Take screenshots of messages.

281
00:15:14,224 --> 00:15:17,254
Preserve the available evidence.

282
00:15:17,254 --> 00:15:18,567
Rather than simply saying,

283
00:15:18,567 --> 00:15:22,254
“They called many times,” your complaint is clearer when you can explain,

284
00:15:22,254 --> 00:15:26,254
“On this date, at this time, this number called and said this.”

285
00:15:26,254 --> 00:15:29,254
Send a written complaint to the bank's grievance team.

286
00:15:29,254 --> 00:15:32,254
Explain the recovery agency's conduct.

287
00:15:32,254 --> 00:15:34,254
Get a complaint reference number.

288
00:15:34,254 --> 00:15:38,394
If the bank rejects your complaint, the response is unsatisfactory,

289
00:15:38,394 --> 00:15:41,237
or you receive no response within thirty days,

290
00:15:41,237 --> 00:15:45,254
you may escalate it through the applicable RBI Ombudsman process.

291
00:15:45,254 --> 00:15:49,754
The RBI Complaint Management System's official address

292
00:15:49,754 --> 00:15:52,254
is cms dot rbi dot org dot in.

293
00:15:52,254 --> 00:15:54,414
Remember this distinction.

294
00:15:54,414 --> 00:15:57,414
A harassment complaint concerns recovery conduct.

295
00:15:57,414 --> 00:15:59,414
It does not cancel the debt.

296
00:15:59,414 --> 00:16:02,414
Nor does it guarantee approval of a settlement discount.

297
00:16:02,414 --> 00:16:07,414
But you have the right to ask to be treated fairly.

298
00:16:07,414 --> 00:16:12,454
What if nonstop calls are disrupting daily life?

299
00:16:12,454 --> 00:16:14,454
Use your phone settings.

300
00:16:14,454 --> 00:16:17,454
You can block known abusive numbers.

301
00:16:17,454 --> 00:16:19,454
Enable spam filters.

302
00:16:19,454 --> 00:16:23,454
You can turn on WhatsApp's Silence Unknown Callers option.

303
00:16:23,454 --> 00:16:26,454
But keep a verified communication channel open.

304
00:16:26,454 --> 00:16:28,454
Check the bank's emails.

305
00:16:28,454 --> 00:16:30,454
Collect official letters.

306
00:16:30,454 --> 00:16:36,035
Silencing unknown calls may also make you miss job, hospital, or delivery calls,

307
00:16:36,035 --> 00:16:36,454
right?

308
00:16:36,454 --> 00:16:40,454
Choose settings that suit your daily needs.

309
00:16:40,454 --> 00:16:42,454
Set aside a fixed time.

310
00:16:42,454 --> 00:16:47,454
Check bank communications then and respond to those that need a reply.

311
00:16:47,454 --> 00:16:52,153
A routine helps you avoid being emotionally drained by calls throughout the day.

312
00:16:52,153 --> 00:16:56,753
“If I do not answer the calls, will the file close after sixty days?”

313
00:16:57,773 --> 00:16:58,973
There is no such guarantee.

314
00:16:59,273 --> 00:17:02,273
The recovery agency may change. The bank's team may change.

315
00:17:02,473 --> 00:17:04,573
Calls may decrease and then increase again.

316
00:17:04,773 --> 00:17:09,373
But a change in the agency's assignment does not make the debt disappear.

317
00:17:09,773 --> 00:17:12,073
Your plan should not depend on silence.

318
00:17:12,473 --> 00:17:15,939
It should depend on a budget, written communication, evidence,

319
00:17:15,939 --> 00:17:17,673
and verified repayment options.

320
00:17:18,173 --> 00:17:23,273
Now, let us see what happens to the account from the due date onwards.

321
00:17:23,773 --> 00:17:25,373
Your statement has a due date.

322
00:17:25,573 --> 00:17:29,473
By that date, you need to pay the full amount or the required minimum amount.

323
00:17:29,973 --> 00:17:33,373
If you do not pay the full bill, applicable finance charges may arise.

324
00:17:33,773 --> 00:17:37,573
If you do not fully pay the minimum amount either, the account becomes overdue.

325
00:17:38,073 --> 00:17:42,220
RBI rules say the credit card account must be past due for more than three

326
00:17:42,220 --> 00:17:46,873
days before late payment charges can be levied or the account reported as past due.

327
00:17:47,173 --> 00:17:51,073
But the days-past-due calculation starts from the original due date.

328
00:17:51,373 --> 00:17:54,573
So, do not treat those extra three days as a new due date.

329
00:17:55,073 --> 00:17:57,073
Do not plan to delay the payment.

330
00:17:57,573 --> 00:18:00,573
As the delay continues, collection follow-up may increase.

331
00:18:00,773 --> 00:18:02,273
Account restrictions may apply.

332
00:18:02,573 --> 00:18:04,373
Your credit report may be affected.

333
00:18:04,873 --> 00:18:08,773
Many people assume, “There will be no problem until ninety days.”

334
00:18:09,073 --> 00:18:13,388
That is incorrect. Even before NPA classification, there can be overdue reporting,

335
00:18:13,388 --> 00:18:15,073
charges, and recovery follow-up.

336
00:18:15,573 --> 00:18:16,492
Under RBI rules,

337
00:18:16,492 --> 00:18:22,986
if the minimum amount due shown in your statement is not fully paid within ninety days from the payment due date,

338
00:18:22,986 --> 00:18:25,573
the credit card account is treated as an NPA.

339
00:18:26,073 --> 00:18:27,573
What does NPA mean?

340
00:18:27,773 --> 00:18:32,073
In the bank's asset classification, the account has become non-performing.

341
00:18:32,273 --> 00:18:35,073
Bank accounting and provisioning rules apply.

342
00:18:35,273 --> 00:18:39,073
But from your perspective, does NPA classification mean you no longer need to pay?

343
00:18:39,273 --> 00:18:42,391
No. Similarly, if the bank offers EMI conversion,

344
00:18:42,391 --> 00:18:45,573
look at the details before immediately saying yes.

345
00:18:45,573 --> 00:18:49,573
What is the monthly EMI, interest rate, and tenure?

346
00:18:49,773 --> 00:18:52,573
Is there a processing fee? What is the total repayment?

347
00:18:52,773 --> 00:18:54,273
Here is the most important question.

348
00:18:54,573 --> 00:18:58,073
Can you genuinely afford that EMI every month?

349
00:18:58,273 --> 00:19:02,044
Taking an unaffordable EMI just to escape credit card pressure can

350
00:19:02,044 --> 00:19:05,073
bring the same problem back in a new form next month.

351
00:19:05,273 --> 00:19:08,073
An affordable repayment plan may be useful.

352
00:19:08,273 --> 00:19:11,073
So, understand the offer before deciding.

353
00:19:11,273 --> 00:19:12,573
Now, let us talk about write-off.

354
00:19:13,073 --> 00:19:16,073
Many people feel relieved when they hear that word.

355
00:19:16,273 --> 00:19:18,073
“Does that mean the bank has removed my debt?”

356
00:19:18,273 --> 00:19:19,573
That is where the confusion lies.

357
00:19:19,773 --> 00:19:22,573
A technical write-off is generally an accounting action.

358
00:19:22,773 --> 00:19:24,573
The treatment in the bank's books may change.

359
00:19:24,773 --> 00:19:28,073
But the claim against the borrower is not automatically waived.

360
00:19:28,273 --> 00:19:30,047
Recovery may continue.

361
00:19:30,047 --> 00:19:32,984
There is no universal rule that every card must

362
00:19:32,984 --> 00:19:36,047
be written off after one hundred and eighty days.

363
00:19:36,047 --> 00:19:40,047
The timing depends on the issuer's policy and the facts of the account.

364
00:19:40,047 --> 00:19:45,047
Waiting for write-off does not guarantee a large discount.

365
00:19:45,047 --> 00:19:49,047
When you are struggling, you can discuss workable options with the bank immediately.

366
00:19:49,047 --> 00:19:54,047
You do not necessarily have to wait for write-off to request a settlement.

367
00:19:54,047 --> 00:19:59,267
Now, let us discuss differences between banks.

368
00:19:59,267 --> 00:20:07,267
SBI Card, HDFC, ICICI, Axis, YES Bank, Kotak, RBL, and IDFC FIRST.

369
00:20:07,267 --> 00:20:10,357
Every issuer's process may be different.

370
00:20:10,357 --> 00:20:14,357
Even within one bank, different accounts may receive different offers.

371
00:20:14,357 --> 00:20:18,357
“My friend settled at twenty-five percent, so I should get the same.”

372
00:20:18,357 --> 00:20:22,357
Do not get fixated on that. Your friend's account may have a different age.

373
00:20:22,357 --> 00:20:24,357
The outstanding balance's breakdown may differ.

374
00:20:24,357 --> 00:20:26,357
Their financial situation may be different.

375
00:20:26,357 --> 00:20:28,357
The approval policy may differ too.

376
00:20:28,357 --> 00:20:33,357
Do not treat a settlement percentage mentioned online as a promise for your case.

377
00:20:33,357 --> 00:20:37,843
Look at the verified written offer from your bank, consider what you can afford,

378
00:20:37,843 --> 00:20:39,357
and discuss it accordingly.

379
00:20:39,357 --> 00:20:43,357
A friendly caller does not automatically mean the offer is genuine.

380
00:20:43,357 --> 00:20:47,357
And a rude caller is not a reason to ignore the account details.

381
00:20:47,357 --> 00:20:49,357
Verify the process.

382
00:20:49,357 --> 00:20:52,357
Do not make a financial decision based on someone's tone.

383
00:20:52,357 --> 00:20:57,350
Okay. What does settlement actually mean?

384
00:20:57,350 --> 00:21:00,532
The bank agrees to accept part of its claimed

385
00:21:00,532 --> 00:21:04,350
dues and waive the remaining claim under agreed terms.

386
00:21:04,350 --> 00:21:06,350
It is a mutual agreement.

387
00:21:06,350 --> 00:21:08,350
Your request alone is not enough.

388
00:21:08,350 --> 00:21:10,350
The bank's approval is needed too.

389
00:21:10,350 --> 00:21:14,174
You can make a realistic proposal based on your income, hardship,

390
00:21:14,174 --> 00:21:15,350
and available funds.

391
00:21:15,350 --> 00:21:18,350
“This is the amount I can arrange at present.

392
00:21:18,350 --> 00:21:20,350
I cannot commit to anything more.

393
00:21:20,350 --> 00:21:23,350
Please consider a full and final settlement,” you can ask.

394
00:21:23,350 --> 00:21:26,440
But borrowing again at very high interest to fund

395
00:21:26,440 --> 00:21:30,350
the settlement risks moving you from one problem into another.

396
00:21:30,350 --> 00:21:33,350
The settlement amount must be affordable.

397
00:21:33,350 --> 00:21:35,350
The payment deadline must be realistic.

398
00:21:35,350 --> 00:21:37,350
Here is an example.

399
00:21:37,350 --> 00:21:39,350
Suppose your outstanding amount is one lakh.

400
00:21:39,350 --> 00:21:43,350
A caller says, “Pay thirty thousand and we will close it.”

401
00:21:43,350 --> 00:21:45,350
That sounds like a relief, right?

402
00:21:45,350 --> 00:21:48,350
But do not make the payment immediately out of excitement.

403
00:21:48,350 --> 00:21:52,350
First, ask, “Can you send the official settlement letter?

404
00:21:52,350 --> 00:21:55,350
Can I verify this offer through the bank's customer care?”

405
00:21:55,350 --> 00:21:58,350
The offer's authenticity matters more than its amount.

406
00:21:58,350 --> 00:22:02,513
The settlement letter must clearly identify your name and account,

407
00:22:02,513 --> 00:22:07,307
the agreed amount, payment dates, and the schedule if there are instalments.

408
00:22:07,307 --> 00:22:09,740
If you pay the agreed amount fully and on time,

409
00:22:09,740 --> 00:22:11,707
how will the remaining dues be waived?

410
00:22:11,707 --> 00:22:13,307
Will there be any further claim?

411
00:22:13,307 --> 00:22:14,907
How will the account be reported?

412
00:22:14,907 --> 00:22:16,507
You need to understand all of this.

413
00:22:16,507 --> 00:22:20,177
Use communication from an official bank channel or

414
00:22:20,177 --> 00:22:24,067
an authorised settlement letter verified by the bank.

415
00:22:24,067 --> 00:22:27,267
Do not trust a WhatsApp screenshot alone.

416
00:22:27,267 --> 00:22:31,867
What if someone says, “Make a small payment first, and the letter will follow”?

417
00:22:32,267 --> 00:22:35,867
Confirm in writing whether that payment is part of the

418
00:22:35,867 --> 00:22:39,867
settlement or will be adjusted as a regular account payment.

419
00:22:39,867 --> 00:22:45,096
If money you pay believing it is a settlement is recorded as an ordinary part payment,

420
00:22:45,096 --> 00:22:47,467
that creates a misunderstanding, right?

421
00:22:47,467 --> 00:22:50,467
Get clarity before making the payment.

422
00:22:50,467 --> 00:22:53,927
Use only payment channels authorised by the bank.

423
00:22:53,927 --> 00:22:58,927
The official app, website, or a payment method the bank has confirmed.

424
00:22:58,927 --> 00:23:01,927
Do not transfer money to an agent's personal UPI account.

425
00:23:01,927 --> 00:23:03,927
Do not hand over cash.

426
00:23:03,927 --> 00:23:05,927
Save the payment receipt.

427
00:23:05,927 --> 00:23:10,927
If your agreement has multiple instalments, carefully follow the due dates.

428
00:23:10,927 --> 00:23:15,927
Understand beforehand how missing an instalment would affect the offer.

429
00:23:15,927 --> 00:23:17,423
After completing payment,

430
00:23:17,423 --> 00:23:22,927
obtain written confirmation and the applicable No Dues or settlement completion certificate.

431
00:23:22,927 --> 00:23:25,874
If a court recovery case is already pending,

432
00:23:25,874 --> 00:23:30,027
confirm how those proceedings will be closed after settlement.

433
00:23:30,027 --> 00:23:34,027
A telephone assurance that “We will handle everything” is not enough.

434
00:23:34,027 --> 00:23:36,287
What about Lok Adalat?

435
00:23:36,287 --> 00:23:39,287
The name itself makes some people nervous: “Do I have to go to court?

436
00:23:39,287 --> 00:23:41,287
What will they ask me there?”

437
00:23:41,287 --> 00:23:44,191
A regular Lok Adalat offers an opportunity for

438
00:23:44,191 --> 00:23:47,347
the parties to reach a mutually agreed settlement.

439
00:23:47,347 --> 00:23:51,347
Eligible pending cases and pre-litigation disputes may also be brought there.

440
00:23:51,347 --> 00:23:55,347
They will explain the proposal. Understand the terms.

441
00:23:55,347 --> 00:23:57,347
Check whether they are affordable for you.

442
00:23:57,347 --> 00:24:01,347
Going there does not mean you have to accept any offer you receive.

443
00:24:01,347 --> 00:24:05,347
Consent matters in a regular Lok Adalat settlement.

444
00:24:05,347 --> 00:24:09,533
An award based on an agreed settlement is final and binding,

445
00:24:09,533 --> 00:24:11,347
like a civil court decree.

446
00:24:11,347 --> 00:24:13,347
There is no ordinary appeal.

447
00:24:13,347 --> 00:24:19,347
So, understand the amount, dates, and consequences clearly before signing.

448
00:24:19,347 --> 00:24:22,347
If you do not understand the terms, ask.

449
00:24:22,347 --> 00:24:25,347
“Will there be any further dues after I pay this amount?

450
00:24:25,347 --> 00:24:27,347
What happens if I miss the payment deadline?

451
00:24:27,347 --> 00:24:30,347
What status will appear in my credit report?”

452
00:24:30,347 --> 00:24:32,347
There is nothing wrong with asking these questions.

453
00:24:32,347 --> 00:24:35,347
Getting clarity about your case is your responsibility.

454
00:24:35,347 --> 00:24:40,314
Now, a question people often ask after settlement.

455
00:24:40,314 --> 00:24:42,314
“Is my CIBIL score ruined?

456
00:24:42,314 --> 00:24:44,314
Will I ever get a loan again?”

457
00:24:44,314 --> 00:24:46,314
You do not have to assume that.

458
00:24:46,314 --> 00:24:50,314
But settlement can affect your credit profile.

459
00:24:50,314 --> 00:24:52,268
Understand that honestly.

460
00:24:52,308 --> 00:24:57,634
“Settled” generally indicates a payment below the full contractual dues,

461
00:24:57,634 --> 00:24:59,928
made with the lender's consent.

462
00:25:00,708 --> 00:25:02,218
“Closed” is a different status,

463
00:25:02,218 --> 00:25:04,848
associated with an account that has been fully repaid.

464
00:25:05,468 --> 00:25:08,128
Lenders may view a “Settled” status negatively.

465
00:25:08,708 --> 00:25:11,228
It can affect future loan or card approvals.

466
00:25:11,928 --> 00:25:17,268
Receiving a No Dues Certificate does not mean your credit report must show “Closed”.

467
00:25:17,868 --> 00:25:21,848
Settlement completion and credit reporting status are two different things.

468
00:25:22,268 --> 00:25:24,268
So, can you rebuild your credit?

469
00:25:24,268 --> 00:25:27,268
Yes, you can. But there is no instant reset.

470
00:25:27,268 --> 00:25:29,268
First, stabilise your income.

471
00:25:29,268 --> 00:25:31,268
Make your monthly budget manageable.

472
00:25:31,268 --> 00:25:34,268
Build a small emergency fund.

473
00:25:34,268 --> 00:25:36,543
Just because you feel relieved that the debt has been cleared,

474
00:25:36,543 --> 00:25:38,268
you do not need to take new credit immediately.

475
00:25:38,268 --> 00:25:43,268
Later, if it is suitable for you, you can consider an FD-backed secured credit card.

476
00:25:43,268 --> 00:25:46,268
That is a card secured against a fixed deposit.

477
00:25:46,268 --> 00:25:51,268
Approval, deposit requirements, and limits depend on the issuer's policy.

478
00:25:51,268 --> 00:25:54,268
Making an FD does not guarantee card approval.

479
00:25:54,268 --> 00:25:59,268
And do not lock up all the savings you need for emergencies just to get a card.

480
00:25:59,268 --> 00:26:04,268
Once you get the card, use it only for small, planned expenses.

481
00:26:04,268 --> 00:26:07,268
Pay the full statement balance by the due date.

482
00:26:07,268 --> 00:26:09,268
Keeping usage low may help.

483
00:26:09,268 --> 00:26:09,965
For example,

484
00:26:09,965 --> 00:26:14,268
one manageable approach might be using ten or twenty percent of the limit.

485
00:26:14,268 --> 00:26:20,268
But using an exact percentage does not guarantee that your score will increase.

486
00:26:20,268 --> 00:26:22,268
What are the most important habits?

487
00:26:22,268 --> 00:26:24,268
Paying on time.

488
00:26:24,268 --> 00:26:26,268
Keeping usage affordable.

489
00:26:26,268 --> 00:26:28,268
Avoiding repeated, unnecessary applications.

490
00:26:28,268 --> 00:26:30,268
Checking your credit report regularly.

491
00:26:30,268 --> 00:26:34,268
After settlement, check whether the bank has updated your report.

492
00:26:34,268 --> 00:26:39,068
If there is an incorrect balance or overdue status, or a duplicate account,

493
00:26:39,068 --> 00:26:42,268
raise a dispute with the lender and credit bureau.

494
00:26:42,268 --> 00:26:46,268
But you cannot remove accurate negative history simply because you do not like it.

495
00:26:46,268 --> 00:26:48,268
One more thing.

496
00:26:48,268 --> 00:26:50,268
“You will reach seven fifty in eighteen months.”

497
00:26:50,268 --> 00:26:52,268
“All your problems will disappear in twenty-four months.”

498
00:26:52,268 --> 00:26:54,268
Do not believe promises like these.

499
00:26:54,268 --> 00:26:58,666
Recovery time depends on your entire credit history, existing accounts,

500
00:26:58,666 --> 00:27:01,268
repayment behaviour, and lender reporting.

501
00:27:01,268 --> 00:27:07,268
Your focus should not be on a magic number, but on sustainable financial habits.

502
00:27:07,268 --> 00:27:09,268
Here is what I want to tell you.

503
00:27:09,268 --> 00:27:13,268
One difficult financial phase does not define your entire life.

504
00:27:13,268 --> 00:27:16,268
Today, you may feel afraid or confused.

505
00:27:16,268 --> 00:27:19,268
You may not know how to tell your family.

506
00:27:19,268 --> 00:27:22,268
But talk to a trusted person.

507
00:27:22,268 --> 00:27:26,268
It could be a family member you feel safe with, or a friend.

508
00:27:26,268 --> 00:27:28,268
You do not have to carry every detail alone.

509
00:27:28,268 --> 00:27:32,562
When you explain your situation, you do not have to begin by saying,

510
00:27:32,562 --> 00:27:34,268
“I have ruined everything.”

511
00:27:34,619 --> 00:27:36,619
“I am facing financial difficulty.

512
00:27:36,859 --> 00:27:39,299
These are my accounts. This is my current income.

513
00:27:39,539 --> 00:27:41,859
This is the plan I want to follow.

514
00:27:42,179 --> 00:27:44,459
I need support.” You can say that.

515
00:27:44,659 --> 00:27:49,339
It is not a weakness. It is a practical step towards facing the problem.

516
00:27:51,849 --> 00:27:56,769
Okay. Let us remember everything we have discussed as a simple eight-step plan.

517
00:27:57,249 --> 00:28:00,049
Step One. List all your accounts.

518
00:28:00,329 --> 00:28:04,689
Calculate your income, essential expenses, and the money available for repayment.

519
00:28:04,889 --> 00:28:06,880
Understand your agreement's terms and any

520
00:28:06,880 --> 00:28:08,969
set-off risk involving your salary account.

521
00:28:09,409 --> 00:28:14,449
Step Two. Explain your hardship through each issuer's official grievance channel.

522
00:28:14,649 --> 00:28:17,289
Ask for affordable repayment options in writing.

523
00:28:17,489 --> 00:28:20,169
Save complaint IDs and replies.

524
00:28:20,689 --> 00:28:24,089
Step Three. Organise recovery communication.

525
00:28:24,289 --> 00:28:26,009
Use spam controls.

526
00:28:26,209 --> 00:28:30,701
But make sure you do not miss verified bank emails, official letters,

527
00:28:30,701 --> 00:28:32,329
or genuine legal notices.

528
00:28:32,889 --> 00:28:37,729
Step Four. Review the cycle of covering old debt with new borrowing.

529
00:28:37,929 --> 00:28:41,889
Understand the benefits and costs of paying the minimum due.

530
00:28:42,089 --> 00:28:44,569
Do not make promises your budget cannot support.

531
00:28:45,089 --> 00:28:49,525
Step Five. If there are threats, humiliation, or abusive messages,

532
00:28:49,525 --> 00:28:51,609
save the evidence and complain.

533
00:28:51,809 --> 00:28:55,329
If necessary, escalate through the RBI complaint process.

534
00:28:55,529 --> 00:28:58,449
In immediate danger, call one one two.

535
00:28:58,969 --> 00:29:04,209
Step Six. Remember the difference between NPA, write-off, and settlement.

536
00:29:04,409 --> 00:29:06,769
Write-off does not cancel the debt.

537
00:29:06,969 --> 00:29:11,209
Discuss workable options instead of blindly waiting for a discount.

538
00:29:11,689 --> 00:29:15,809
Step Seven. If you settle, verify the official offer.

539
00:29:16,009 --> 00:29:20,609
Understand the amount, dates, waiver terms, and credit reporting status.

540
00:29:20,809 --> 00:29:22,729
Pay through an authorised channel and

541
00:29:22,729 --> 00:29:25,169
obtain receipts and confirmation of completion.

542
00:29:25,609 --> 00:29:28,209
Step Eight. Stabilise your income.

543
00:29:28,449 --> 00:29:30,209
Build emergency savings.

544
00:29:30,409 --> 00:29:31,969
Check your credit report.

545
00:29:32,169 --> 00:29:33,298
Then, if necessary,

546
00:29:33,298 --> 00:29:38,409
rebuild your credit profile with suitable secured credit and regular payments in full.

547
00:29:39,119 --> 00:29:41,959
Now, ask yourself one question.

548
00:29:42,359 --> 00:29:46,839
“What is my next step?” You do not need to solve your entire debt today.

549
00:29:47,039 --> 00:29:49,719
But you can take one useful step today, right?

550
00:29:50,039 --> 00:29:51,359
You can list your accounts.

551
00:29:51,559 --> 00:29:53,279
Check your statement's breakdown.

552
00:29:53,479 --> 00:29:54,959
Send a hardship email.

553
00:29:55,279 --> 00:29:57,279
Talk to a trusted person.

554
00:29:57,719 --> 00:30:00,999
Taking one step at a time reduces confusion.

555
00:30:01,199 --> 00:30:03,279
You get clarity about what to do.

556
00:30:03,839 --> 00:30:05,559
You may owe money.

557
00:30:05,759 --> 00:30:09,959
But that does not give anyone permission to treat you disrespectfully.

558
00:30:10,159 --> 00:30:13,039
Handle your responsibilities honestly.

559
00:30:13,239 --> 00:30:15,039
And know your rights too.

560
00:30:15,479 --> 00:30:17,119
There is something personal I want to share.

561
00:30:17,319 --> 00:30:20,279
I am also dealing with this situation right now.

562
00:30:20,479 --> 00:30:23,519
That is why I understand what this pressure feels like.

563
00:30:23,673 --> 00:30:26,313
In the next video, I will talk about my own case.

564
00:30:26,713 --> 00:30:32,407
How I communicate with the banks, which letters I send, the replies I receive,

565
00:30:32,407 --> 00:30:34,233
and the decisions I make.

566
00:30:34,393 --> 00:30:36,033
I will share it all, step by step.

567
00:30:36,433 --> 00:30:40,513
I do not promise that what happened in my case will also happen in yours.

568
00:30:40,833 --> 00:30:43,093
But seeing the real process can help

569
00:30:43,093 --> 00:30:46,233
you ask better questions about your own situation.

570
00:30:46,553 --> 00:30:49,273
Subscribe to the channel so you do not miss that video.

571
00:30:49,553 --> 00:30:52,793
Tap the bell icon and select All notifications.

572
00:30:53,033 --> 00:30:57,073
If you found this video useful, share it with someone who needs it.

573
00:30:57,473 --> 00:31:01,433
They might be quietly struggling with the same stress without telling anyone.

574
00:31:01,753 --> 00:31:06,884
This one video you share may help them think calmly, ask for help,

575
00:31:06,884 --> 00:31:08,673
and take the next step.

576
00:31:08,793 --> 00:31:09,633
It could make a difference.
